<title>ESTONIA: HANSA APPROVES Q1 RESULTS, ELECTS NEW AUDITOR.</title>
<headline>HANSA APPROVES Q1 RESULTS, ELECTS NEW AUDITOR.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hansapank's council on Monday evening approved its first quarter results and elected a new auditor, Hannes Tamjarv, the council's chairman, told Reuters on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The board elected Price Waterhouse to be the bank's new auditor, replacing KPMG Estonia, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;Hansapank has had only had one auditor so far and we thought that it was suitable to change,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Hansapank said it had a net profit of 136.1 million kroons in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
